---
title: FOSSBilling File Structure
description: Understanding how FOSSBilling organizes its code and where things live.
---

FOSSBilling's structure can feel unusual if you are coming from modern frameworks like Laravel or Symfony. This guide shows where the main pieces live and what each directory is responsible for.

## Source Code

All source code lives in the `/src` directory.

### `/src/data`

Runtime data storage:
- **Cache** — Compiled templates, API responses
- **Logs** — Application logs and error logs
- **Uploads** — User-uploaded files (`/data/uploads`)

This directory should be writable by the web server.

### `/src/install`

The installation wizard. Automatically deleted after installation unless `APP_ENV=dev` is set.

### `/src/library`

Core PHP classes and business logic.

#### `/src/library/Api`

Core API files including the JavaScript wrapper (`API.js`). [See the wrapper docs](/extensions-and-development/javascript/).

#### `/src/library/Box`

Legacy classes inherited from BoxBilling. Some have been migrated to `FOSSBilling/`:

| File | Status |
|------|--------|
| `Box/Exception.php` | Removed |
| `Box/Mod.php` | Removed — replaced by `FOSSBilling/Module.php` |
| `Box/Paginator.php` | Removed — replaced by `FOSSBilling/Paginator.php` |
| `Box/TwigExtensions.php` | Removed — replaced by `FOSSBilling/Twig/` |
| `Box/TwigLoader.php` | Removed — replaced by `FOSSBilling/Twig/` |
| `Box/Translate.php` | Still present |

#### `/src/library/FOSSBilling`

New or rewritten classes specific to FOSSBilling. Subdirectories reflect the growing architecture:

| Subdirectory | Purpose |
|-------------|---------|
| `Doctrine/` | Doctrine DBAL and ORM factory classes (pairs with RedBean for a dual-ORM approach) |
| `Http/` | `RequestFactory`, `CsvResponseFactory`, HTTP exception handling |
| `Security/` | `RateLimiter`, `RateLimitResult`, `AuthenticationRequiredException`, `RandomizedTimeFloor` |
| `Sanitizer/` | `BrowserHtmlSanitizer` (HTML sanitization via Symfony) |
| `Twig/` | `TwigFactory`, `TwigLoader`, `SandboxedStringRenderer`, custom Twig extensions and filters |
| `Validation/` | API validation utilities |

Key standalone files:
- `Module.php` — Base class for modules (replaces `Box_Mod`)
- `Paginator.php` — Pagination utility (replaces `Box_Paginator`)
- `PaginationOptions.php` — Pagination configuration value object
- `Interfaces/ApiArrayInterface.php`
- `Interfaces/SecurityCheckInterface.php`
- `Interfaces/TimestampInterface.php`
- `Interfaces/WidgetProviderInterface.php`

#### `/src/library/Model`

Database models. Some models have been moved to their respective modules or removed:

| Model | Status |
|-------|--------|
| `Model/ApiRequest.php` | Removed |
| `Model/ClientPasswordResetTable.php` | Removed |
| `Model/Currency.php` | Moved to Currency module |
| `Model/EmailTemplate.php` | Moved to Email module |
| `Model/MassmailerMessage.php` | Moved to Massmailer module |
| `Model/Post.php` | Moved to Post module |
| `Model/ProductMembership.php` | Removed |
| `Model/ServiceMembership.php` | Removed |

#### `/src/library/Payment`

Payment gateway adapters. If you're building a payment gateway, look in `/src/library/Payment/Adapter/`.

[Guide: Creating a Payment Gateway](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-payment-gateway/)

#### `/src/library/Registrar`

Domain registrar adapters for domain reselling. Check `/src/library/Registrar/Adapter/`.

[Guide: Creating a Registrar Integration](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-registrar-integration/)

#### `/src/library/Server`

Server manager adapters for hosting control panels (cPanel, Plesk, HestiaCP, etc.).

{% aside type="note" %}
These are for shared hosting control panels. For VPS or game servers, consider creating a product module instead.
{% /aside %}

[Guide: Creating a Server Manager](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-server-manager/)

### `/src/locale`

Translations as a Git submodule. Pointing to [github.com/FOSSBilling/locale](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/locale).

### `/src/modules`

All modules live here. Each module is a self-contained unit of functionality.

A typical module structure:

```
ModuleName/
├── Api/
│   ├── Admin.php       # Admin API endpoints
│   ├── Client.php      # Client API endpoints
│   └── Guest.php       # Guest/public API endpoints
├── Controller/
│   ├── Admin.php       # Admin routes/controllers
│   ├── Client.php      # Client routes/controllers
│   └── Guest.php       # Guest routes/controllers
├── templates/          # Module templates (was html_* in 0.7.x)
│   ├── admin/          # Admin panel templates
│   ├── client/         # Client area templates
│   └── email/          # Email templates
├── manifest.json       # Module metadata
└── Service.php         # Business logic (not exposed via API)
```

{% aside type="caution" %}
The old `html_admin/`, `html_client/`, and `html_email/` directories have been removed. Custom modules **must** use the `templates/{admin,client,email}/` structure.
{% /aside %}

[Guide: Creating a Module](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-module/)

### `/src/themes`

All installed themes.

Theme structure:

```
theme-name/
├── assets/                 # CSS, JS, images (built via esbuild, not webpack)
├── config/
│   └── settings.html.twig       # Theme settings UI
├── html/                   # Twig templates
│   └── layouts/            # Base layouts
├── html_custom/            # User overrides (overrides take priority)
└── manifest.json           # Theme metadata
```

The `html_custom/` folder lets users override templates without editing the theme directly.

[Guide: Creating a Theme](/extensions-and-development/guides/creating-a-theme/)

